  "name": "Reaper: Ghost Form cannot apply after an indoor corpse reclaim (#6437)",
  "contract": "Ghost Form561083 permits casting while dead but is usable only outdoors. The native dead-target guard prevents an applied aura until resurrection; a completed dead cast can leave an owned aura pending. Corpse reclaim indoors must discard that non-passive outdoor-only owned aura, so it cannot apply after resurrection or reappear on a later outdoor transition. An outdoor corpse reclaim preserves the permitted form and its authored60% speed. Living indoor casting is rejected with93 and an ordinary living outdoor-to-indoor transition removes the form. The indoor location is native Innkeeper Firebrew5111/guid1745 at (-4840.67,-857.094,501.997), with vmap indoor checks enabled. Each dead cast is observed as a new SpellGo relative to a pre-cast snapshot before returning to the corpse. Six seconds after reclaim cover delayed aura target-map updates. Teleports position the fixture only; casts, spirit release and corpse reclaim use normal native handlers. CMSG_RECLAIM_CORPSE466 ignores its GUID field and validates the actual corpse, delay and distance. Acquisition of561083 is outside this aura-lifecycle regression.",
